This package contains some useful utilities if you have a os9-net running."rex node command" executes a command on the os9-net host named node with thegroup.user id of the rex command. For that reason it is advised that allpassword files on your os9-net are identical."rexd" is the daemon needed on the remote machine to service the rex requests."rexdc" is the real server on the remote machine, forked by "rexd". All youhave to do, is to put a line like 'rexd &' in your startup file."chp node" is used to make a remote login over os9-net. It is equivalent to"rex node login" and only included for compatibility with the original os9-netpackage."remdate node" ask the remote host "node" for his current time and sets thelocal time to that value.mtsmon or tsmon is no longer needed with this package!Have fun,Peter